From: wu <wuc8974@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:21:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] feat(pqc-m1): ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) key storage, sign,
 verify

- src/infra/mldsa65-key-storage.ts: MLDSA65-* storage layer
  - generateMlDsa65Keypair(): FIPS 204 keygen via @noble/post-quantum
  - encodeMlDsa65{Public,Secret}Key: "MLDSA65-*-KEY:" + base64url(raw)
  - decodeMlDsa65{Public,Secret}Key: throws on missing prefix, bad base64url,
    wrong length (1952 pub / 4032 sec)
  - signMlDsa65Payload: strips prefix, signs raw payload, returns base64url
  - verifyMlDsa65Signature: returns false on any failure, throws only on
    non-string programmer-error inputs
  - tryDecode*Raw: non-throwing variant for legacy migration probes
- src/infra/mldsa65-key-storage.test.ts: 29 invariants
  - keypair generation (length 1952/4032, non-zero entropy, no collision)
  - encode/decode round-trip (pub, sec, base64url validity)
  - bad input rejection (wrong length, non-typed-array, missing prefix,
    malformed base64url, empty body)
  - sign/verify across 8 payload variants including UTF-8 boundary
  - signature exact length 3309 bytes
  - non-determinism (hedged mode, FIPS 204 section 5.3)
  - tamper detection: 1-byte flip, wrong pk, wrong length, truncated sig,
    malformed base64url, bad prefix
  - cross-key isolation: A's sig never verifies under B's pk
  - throw on programmer-error inputs (null publicKey / secretKey)
- src/infra/device-identity.ts: ESM .js import fix for the
  @noble/post-quantum/ml-dsa module referenced from danteng's c87a41c1
  baseline. TypeScript ESM requires the .js extension to resolve the
  TS source declaration.

Whitepaper section: 2.1.1 (FIPS 204 device identity)
pnpm tsgo:core: 0 new errors introduced (8 pre-existing errors in
src/process/exec-runner.ts, src/secrets/trusted-plan-path.ts,
src/snapshot/local-repository.ts are unchanged from upstream).
